  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened constituents&apos; capacity to analyse labour market indicators targeting better employment services and high impact partnerships for promoting decent work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO in Brazil is collaborating with national constituents to enhance decent work and social justice through initiatives focused on data-driven policy development using PNAD-C (continuous household survey) and Census 2022 data, utilizing strategic insights from the Smartlab for labour and human rights policies. Further efforts include developing sustainable mining models, promoting supply chain due diligence, creating occupational projections to inform education and training policies, applying systemic territorial analysis for productive inclusion and investment guidance, fostering green jobs and sustainable development in infrastructure projects, and enhancing ILO&apos;s digital outreach. These actions align with SDG 8.3, promoting development-oriented policies for decent job creation, entrepreneurship, and the formalization of micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises, fostering inclusive growth and an equitable recovery by 2025. Key beneficiaries and strategic partners in these efforts are federal, state, and municipal governments, utilizing data for public policies and decision-making. Also involved are government agents, including labour public prosecutors from the Labour Prosecutors Office (MPT), who will use Smartlab to advance labor and human rights policies.</narrative>
  </description>
